## What We Are Building

A first-class refactor of shot identity, requested by the Director as "АРХИВАЖНО".
Root cause of chronic numbering chaos (SH10, SH12/13/14, E11 "18/20 not found"):
the system never decided what a shot's IDENTITY is. The id was a positional compound
`SS-S15-E12-A2-SC07-SH12` with the UNSTABLE scene baked in — scene = POSITION, drifts
on board re-version / agent re-number / human "по аналогии с SH10". Weak models latch
the drifting prefix → shots "lost". ~21 band-aids normalized the prefix at scattered
doors; the class never died.

Target (Director q2): identity = **`S{season}-E{episode}-SH{number}`** (e.g. `S15-E12-SH07`)
— NO `SS`, NO act, NO scene. Number assigned by POSITION in code (model-independent),
frozen forever (delete→gap, never re-pack), validator HALTs on any non-canonical id.
Act/scene become derived display, not shown (q8). Old episodes E01–E12 = LEGACY (frozen,
opaque). New scheme starts E13+. No heavy data migration. Net subtractive (delete the
band-aids). Decisions locked in Director Q&A q1–q10 (2026-06-26).

Full plan: `~/.claude/plans/shot-identity-refactor-S-E-SH.md`.
Decision memory: `~/.claude/projects/C--SandyStudio/memory/shot_identity_refactor_decision.md`.

